# Round 76: vec_loop vectorized loops with LOOP-CARRIED buffer
# dependencies -- the first strike on the SIMD recognizers since their
# construction. Two-sided, both executed: a self-read at negative offset
# (`b[i] is b[i-1] + 1`, the prefix chain) read stale lanes (AOT
# 1 2 1 2... vs the VM's 1 2 3 4...), and a cross-statement read at +1 of
# a buffer the loop writes inverted the other way -- both rc 0. The
# recognizer's "always correct regardless of the static analysis" comment
# was refuted: the runtime guard defends bounds, not dependence. The rule
# now: a NONZERO-offset read of any buffer the loop WRITES bails to the
# scalar path (byte-exact by construction); zero-offset reads of written
# buffers stay vectorized (per-statement emission preserves same-lane
# ordering both directions), and offset reads of UNWRITTEN buffers keep
# the stencil path (t13 pins that half).
n is 12
b is buffer of n
i is 0
loop while i < n:
    b[i] is b[i - 1] + 1
    i is i + 1
j is 0
loop while j < n:
    print of b[j]
    j is j + 1
c is buffer of n
d is buffer of n
m is n - 1
k is 0
loop while k < m:
    c[k] is k * 1.0
    d[k] is c[k + 1] * 10
    k is k + 1
q is 0
loop while q < m:
    print of d[q]
    q is q + 1
